{
  "id": "w-fragen",
  "name": "Wh- questions: what, where, when, who",
  "level": "A1",
  "subtitle": "A Wh- question starts with a question word: what, where, when, who, why or how. After it comes do, does or a form of be, then the subject: Where do you live? Where is the bank?",
  "briefMarks": ["what","where","when","who","why","how"],
  "source": "EnglishAcademy original English text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-10-29)",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      {
        "text": "Wh- word",
        "variant": "verb"
      },
      {
        "text": "do / does / is / are",
        "variant": "prep"
      },
      {
        "text": "subject"
      },
      {
        "text": "verb + rest?"
      }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "<span class=\"vp-verb\">Where</span> <span class=\"vp-prep\">do</span> you live? — <span class=\"vp-verb\">What</span> <span class=\"vp-prep\">is</span> your name? — <span class=\"vp-verb\">When</span> <span class=\"vp-prep\">does</span> the film start?",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "With most verbs: <strong>Wh- word + do/does + subject + base verb</strong>.<br><em>Where do you work? What does she want? When do they leave?</em><br><strong>does</strong> already shows the -s, so the main verb has none.<br>✗ <em>Where you live?</em> → ✓ <em>Where do you live?</em><br>✗ <em>What does she wants?</em> → ✓ <em>What does she want?</em>",
        "tag": "do / does"
      },
      {
        "html": "With <strong>be</strong>: <strong>Wh- word + am/is/are + subject</strong>. There is no do.<br><em>What is your name? Where are you from? How old is he?</em><br>✗ <em>Why you are late?</em> → ✓ <em>Why are you late?</em>",
        "tag": "With be"
      },
      {
        "html": "When <strong>who</strong> or <strong>what</strong> is the subject, there is no do or does. The verb takes -s.<br><em>Who lives next door? — Mr Patel.</em><br><em>What happens next? — We eat.</em><br>✗ <em>Who does live next door?</em> → ✓ <em>Who lives next door?</em>",
        "tag": "Who as subject"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>what</strong> = thing · <strong>who</strong> = person · <strong>where</strong> = place · <strong>when</strong> = time · <strong>why</strong> = reason (answer: <em>because …</em>) · <strong>how</strong> = way<br><em>How</em> also works with other words: <strong>how old</strong> (age), <strong>how much</strong> (price, uncountable things), <strong>how many</strong> (number of things).",
        "tag": "Meanings"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>which</strong> = choose from a few: <em>Which bus goes to York?</em><br><strong>whose</strong> = owner: <em>Whose bag is this? — It's Priya's.</em><br><strong>how many</strong> + plural noun: <em>How many brothers do you have?</em><br><strong>how much</strong> + uncountable noun or price: <em>How much milk do we need? How much is the ticket?</em><br>✗ <em>How many brother do you have?</em> → ✓ <em>How many brothers do you have?</em>",
        "tag": "which, whose, how many"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Do not mix up <strong>who</strong> (a person: <em>Who is that?</em>), <strong>whose</strong> (the owner: <em>Whose coat is that?</em>) and <strong>which</strong> (a choice: <em>Which coat do you want?</em>). For questions that you answer with yes or no, see <a href=\"/ja-nein-fragen\">yes/no questions</a>. For the verb forms, see the <a href=\"/praesens\">present simple</a>.",
